  "ingredients": [
    "2 pounds catfish fillets",
    "4 cups water",
    "2 medium onions, finely chopped",
    "salt and ground black pepper to taste",
    "2 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
    "2 teaspoons curry powder",
    "2 tablespoons butter, at room temperature",
    "1 tablespoon chopped fresh parsley",
    "4 cups hot cooked rice"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/UsPvmFBQ3sI_GxZjgCiBUTCqXLQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-01-b6ae01d3eae64aed83032a49431b2a86.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rinse fillets under cold water and cut into 2-inch pieces.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/R-4k4IOcLK8VnXJw1YJXtip_yok=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-02-fbf215c84187472e8e3890c10bf5c28e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place catfish into a medium saucepan and add water, onions, salt, and pepper. Bring to a boil; reduce heat, and simmer until fish is tender but not breaking apart, about 8 minutes. Transfer fish to a serving platter using a slotted spoon and cover with foil to keep warm.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/M9NhTp9B0TNQbJgGNUiRWLy4hzE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-03-dab6de40c61f4905acadf56a91bdceea.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring the cooking liquid in the saucepan to a boil; continue to boil until it reduces to 1 cup, then keep warm over low heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/5sldnYdVpnkFROomFXj_rfMFrdI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-04-bafe80e3aa224ac5b0c1fecd163ff720.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine flour, curry, and butter in a small bowl. Mix with a fork or fingertips to form a smooth paste. Roll teaspoon-sized bits of paste into balls.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/WCXbt6CGy2yzsvp1lJxwoNeBTBQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-05-311636ddb5bd4649a008998ee15a29ec.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Return the cooking liquid to a simmer. While stirring slowly and continuously, drop the balls into the liquid one at a time, letting each one dissolve before adding the next. Cook until the sauce returns just to a boil and thickens to the consistency of gravy, about 5 minutes. Check the seasoning.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/FU9tDjzpzkcq2QmzD6ONbqx_92A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-06-a2772eced68a4fffbc3e70cfecf99aff.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the gravy over the fish and boiled rice, sprinkle some parsley on top, and serve hot.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/7ufHlpU_4W9TstWhMHexC0Cozbk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-388304-catfish-curry-VAT-4x3-step-07-2ecfa7c0bfff44f4ab3a0976acf0b0a0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8388304/step_07.webp"
    }
  ],
